c =========================================================================
c PROFILE 3 - SEVERE REFRACTORY RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS (30-qubit CNF)
c =========================================================================
c
c Patient archetype: Mrs L, 55 years old, seropositive RF+/ACPA+ RA
c with active disease despite conventional triple therapy (MTX+SSZ+HCQ),
c now on biologic + JAK inhibitor era management. Includes HTN and
c hypothyroidism comorbidities (typical in long-standing RA).
c
c Epidemiology backing:
c   - 30-40% of RA patients require biologic DMARDs after csDMARD failure
c     (Smolen JS et al. Lancet 2016;388:2023)
c   - Approx 5-10% of RA patients require multiple biologic switches
c   - RA + comorbid hypothyroidism: prevalence 2-3x general population
c     (Cardenas Roldan J et al. Autoimmune Dis 2012;2012:864907)
c
c IMPORTANT CLARIFICATION:
c   - "Conventional triple therapy" = MTX + Sulfasalazine + Hydroxychloroquine
c     (Mottonen NEJM 1996; ACR 2021 conditional recommendation)
c   - The HODDI-discovered "MTX + Tofacitinib + HCQ -> Anaemia" signal
c     in c02 is NOT the same as "triple therapy"; it is a FAERS-derived
c     statistical association captured as an avoidance clause.
c
c Format   : DIMACS WCNF for qaoa_wcnf.py
c Encoding : CJ2 (Ansotegui & Levy 2024; Rodriguez Farres ICCS 2024)
c Qubits   : 30  (12 drug variables + 18 ternary-syndrome clauses)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c DRUG POOL (all FDA-approved; HODDI-verified)
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   x1   Methotrexate         DB00563  L01BA   RA DMARD anchor (11,937)
c                                                ACR 2021 Class I
c   x2   Sulfasalazine        DB00795  A07EC   csDMARD (1,997)
c                                                Triple-therapy partner
c   x3   Hydroxychloroquine   DB01611  P01BA   Antimalarial (3,187)
c                                                Triple-therapy partner
c   x4   Leflunomide          DB01097  L04AK   DHODH inhibitor (2,724)
c                                                csDMARD alternative
c   x5   Folic acid           DB00158  B03BB   MTX rescue (3,239)
c                                                FDA MTX label mandate
c   x6   Prednisone acetate   DB14646  H02AB   GC bridge (11,607)
c                                                ACR 2021 bridge therapy
c   x7   Infliximab           DB00065  L04AB   TNFα mAb (3,460)
c                                                ACR 2021 bDMARD
c   x8   Etanercept           DB00005  L04AB   TNFα soluble R (4,729)
c                                                ACR 2021 bDMARD
c   x9   Tofacitinib          DB08895  L04AF   JAK inhibitor (3,415)
c                                                ACR 2021 tsDMARD
c   x10  Rituximab            DB00073  L01XC   Anti-CD20 mAb (3,460)
c                                                ACR 2021 for refractory RA
c   x11  Naproxen             DB00788  M01AE   NSAID (2,755)
c   x12  Ibuprofen            DB01050  M01AE   NSAID (16,967)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c AVOIDANCE CLAUSES (c01-c06) - HODDI HIGHER-ORDER SIGNALS
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c
c c01 (x1=MTX + x8=Etanercept + x4=Leflunomide -> Platelet decreased)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=176.3, a=4 cases, p_fisher=1.2e-08
c   Triple immunosuppression (DHODH + TNFα + folate antagonism) ->
c   additive myelosuppression
c   FDA labels: all three carry cytopenia warnings
c   Weight: 100 (Tier A)
c
c c02 (x1=MTX + x9=Tofacitinib + x3=HCQ -> Anaemia)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=21.4 (95% CI 7.0-65.4), a=3, p_fisher=4.1e-04
c   NOTE: This is a HODDI-discovered association from FAERS, NOT the
c   conventional "triple therapy" (which is MTX+SSZ+HCQ in c11).
c   Clinical mechanism: cumulative immunomodulation depressing
c   erythropoiesis; Tofacitinib FDA boxed warning includes anemia
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B)
c
c c03 (x1=MTX + x3=HCQ + x11=Naproxen -> Asthma / AERD)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=73.4, a=3, p_fisher=1.0e-05
c   Aspirin-Exacerbated Respiratory Disease - cyclooxygenase inhibition
c   triggering leukotriene-mediated bronchospasm
c   (Annals Allergy 2023, doi:10.1016/j.anai.2023.05.011)
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B - named syndrome)
c
c c04 (x1=MTX + x12=Ibuprofen + x5=Folic acid -> Asthma / AERD)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=39.3, a=3, p_fisher=6.8e-05
c   Same AERD mechanism
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B)
c
c c05 (x1=MTX + x4=Lef + x6=Prednisone -> Platelet decreased)
c   HODDI signal: PRR=106.0, a=3, p_fisher=4.0e-06
c   Triple DMARD + steroid myelosuppression
c   Weight: 50 (Tier B)
c
c c06 (x1=MTX + x7=Infliximab + x10=Rituximab -> Serious infection)
c   Mechanism: ACR 2021 specifically warns against combining two
c   biologic DMARDs (concomitant TNFα blockade + B-cell depletion);
c   FDA Rituximab + Infliximab combination increases severe infection
c   risk by ~3x (Bingham CO et al. Arthritis Rheum 2010)
c   Weight: 100 (Tier A - guideline-prohibited combination)
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c POSITIVE GUIDELINE CLAUSES (c07-c18)
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c
c c07 (x1 v x2 v x3): Conventional triple therapy components
c   ACR 2021 conditional recommendation: MTX + SSZ + HCQ
c   (Mottonen NEJM 1996; O'Dell NEJM 2013;369:307 - TEAR trial)
c   Weight: 30 (Class I)
c
c c08 (x1 v x5 v x6): MTX-anchored regimen with supportive care
c   FDA mandates folic acid with MTX; bridge prednisone for flares
c   Weight: 30
c
c c09 (x7 v x8 v x9): bDMARD or tsDMARD addition after csDMARD failure
c   ACR 2021 Class I: add bDMARD (TNFi preferred) or tsDMARD (JAKi)
c   after inadequate csDMARD response
c   Weight: 30
c
c c10 (x1 v x4 v x2): csDMARD foundation
c   Methotrexate first-line; leflunomide or sulfasalazine if intolerant
c   Weight: 30
c
c c11 (x1 v x3 v x2): Hydroxychloroquine + sulfasalazine + MTX trio
c   Conventional triple therapy (Mottonen NEJM 1996)
c   Weight: 30 (Class I)
c
c c12 (x10 v x9 v x8): Refractory RA escalation options
c   Rituximab, Tofacitinib, Etanercept - alternatives after biologic
c   switching (Bingham 2010; Genovese MC et al. Arthritis Rheum 2008)
c   Weight: 30
c
c c13 (x5 v x6 v x1): MTX-protocol supportive triad
c   FA + GC bridge + MTX
c   Weight: 15 (Class IIa)
c
c c14 (x11 v x12 v x6): Symptomatic flare management
c   NSAID or low-dose GC for breakthrough symptoms
c   Weight: 15
c
c c15 (x7 v x1 v x5): TNFi + MTX combination (preferred bDMARD pairing)
c   ACR 2021: MTX should be continued when adding bDMARD
c   Weight: 15
c
c c16 (x8 v x1 v x5): Etanercept + MTX combination
c   Same evidence base as c15
c   Weight: 15
c
c c17 (x9 v x1 v x5): Tofacitinib + MTX combination
c   Non-inferior to TNFi + MTX (Lee EB NEJM 2014 ORAL Start)
c   Weight: 15
c
c c18 (x2 v x4 v x3): Alternative csDMARD combinations
c   SSZ + Lef + HCQ as alternative trio
c   Weight: 15
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c WEIGHT TOTAL
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   Tier A:    c01, c06                    = 200
c   Tier B:    c02, c03, c04, c05          = 200
c   Class I:   c07,c08,c09,c10,c11,c12     = 180
c   Class IIa: c13,c14,c15,c16,c17,c18     =  90
c   TOTAL = 670
c
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c REFERENCES
c -------------------------------------------------------------------------
c   Mottonen T et al. NEJM 1996;334:1283 (conventional triple therapy)
c   O'Dell JR et al. NEJM 2013;369:307 (TEAR trial)
c   Smolen JS et al. Lancet 2016;388:2023 (RA management)
c   2021 ACR Guideline for Treatment of Rheumatoid Arthritis
c     Fraenkel L et al. Arthritis Care Res 2021;73:924-39
c   Bingham CO et al. Arthritis Rheum 2010;62:9 (bDMARD combination risk)
c   Genovese MC et al. Arthritis Rheum 2008;58:2968 (rituximab in RA)
c   Lee EB et al. NEJM 2014;370:2377 (ORAL Start tofacitinib)
c   AERD review: Annals Allergy 2023, doi:10.1016/j.anai.2023.05.011
c   FDA Labels: MTX, SSZ, HCQ, Leflunomide, Etanercept, Infliximab,
c     Tofacitinib, Rituximab (DailyMed)
c   HODDI: arXiv:2502.06274
c   DDInter 2.0: Nucleic Acids Res 2025;53(D1):D1356
c
c =========================================================================
p wcnf 12 18 101
100 -1 -8 -4 0    c c01  MTX+Etan+Lef -> Platelet decreased (Tier A)
 50 -1 -9 -3 0    c c02  MTX+Tofa+HCQ -> Anaemia (HODDI Tier B)
 50 -1 -3 -11 0   c c03  MTX+HCQ+Naprox -> AERD (Tier B)
 50 -1 -12 -5 0   c c04  MTX+Ibu+FA -> AERD (Tier B)
 50 -1 -4 -6 0    c c05  MTX+Lef+Pred -> Platelet decreased (Tier B)
100 -1 -7 -10 0   c c06  MTX+Inflix+Ritux -> infection (ACR 2021 prohibit)
 30  1  2  3 0    c c07  Conventional triple therapy components
 30  1  5  6 0    c c08  MTX regimen with FA + bridge GC
 30  7  8  9 0    c c09  bDMARD/tsDMARD addition after csDMARD failure
 30  1  4  2 0    c c10  csDMARD foundation (MTX/Lef/SSZ)
 30  1  3  2 0    c c11  Conventional triple therapy trio (Mottonen 1996)
 30  10 9  8 0    c c12  Refractory RA escalation options
 15  5  6  1 0    c c13  MTX-protocol supportive triad
 15  11 12 6 0    c c14  Symptomatic flare mgmt
 15  7  1  5 0    c c15  TNFi+MTX combination (Infliximab)
 15  8  1  5 0    c c16  TNFi+MTX combination (Etanercept)
 15  9  1  5 0    c c17  Tofacitinib+MTX combination (ORAL Start)
 15  2  4  3 0    c c18  Alternative csDMARD trio
